{"dossier":"D05","entry_points":[{"sids":["mm/percpu.c::pcpu_page_first_chunk"],"text":"First-chunk setup needs single-group page granularity, maps one unit per CPU with copied image, frees partial pages on shortage, and aborts when mapping fails."},{"sids":["mm/numa_memblks.c::numa_memblks_init","mm/arch_numa.c::numa_init","mm/arch_numa.c::numa_register_nodes","mm/arch_numa.c::arch_numa_init","mm/arch_numa.c::arch_acpi_numa_init.alt_1","mm/arch_numa.c::arch_acpi_numa_init.alt_2","mm/arch_numa.c::dummy_numa_init","mm/numa_memblks.c::numa_register_meminfo"],"text":"NUMA startup clears state, uses firmware or a synthetic node, cleans and registers extents, validates coverage, onlines nodes, and tears down distances on failure."},{"sids":["mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_class","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_class_init","mm/backing-dev.c::default_bdi_init","mm/backing-dev.c::wb_init"],"text":"Class registration aborts on failure; early init makes a reclaim-capable unbound workqueue, and writeback init links parents, lists, locks, work and stats."}],"exports":[{"sids":["mm/memblock.c::memblock_alloc_internal","mm/memblock.c::memblock_alloc_try_nid","mm/memblock.c::memblock_phys_alloc_try_nid","mm/memblock.c::memblock_prep_allocation","mm/memblock.c::memblock_alloc_range_nid"],"text":"Early boot grants obey a ceiling with retry and null on exhaustion, prefer nodes loosely, divert to slab after init, and run leak plus guest hooks before return."},{"sids":["mm/memblock.c::__memblock_reserve","mm/memblock.c::memblock_setclr_flag","mm/memblock.c::memblock_clear_hotplug","mm/memblock.c::memblock_set_node","mm/memblock.c::memblock_search","mm/memblock.c::memblock_search_pfn_nid","mm/mm_init.c::get_pfn_range_for_nid","mm/memblock.c::memblock_validate_numa_coverage","mm/memblock.c::memblock_phys_mem_size"],"text":"Reservation installs disjoint gaps with growth and coalescing, retags only affected spans, resolves owners via ordered search, and checks NUMA coverage against loss limits."},{"sids":["mm/numa_memblks.c::numa_add_memblk","mm/numa_memblks.c::numa_register_meminfo","mm/numa.c::alloc_node_data","mm/arch_numa.c::setup_node_data","mm/percpu.c::pcpu_fc_alloc","mm/percpu.c::pcpu_fc_free"],"text":"NUMA ranges are recorded then published after cleaning; node stores prefer local backing with memoryless fallback, and percpu pages prefer platform nodes with pool release."},{"sids":["mm/page-writeback.c::wb_calc_thresh","mm/page-writeback.c::cgwb_calc_thresh","mm/memcontrol.c::mem_cgroup_wb_domain","mm/memcontrol.c::mem_cgroup_wb_stats","mm/page-writeback.c::global_dirty_limits","mm/page-writeback.c::bdi_get_min_bytes","mm/page-writeback.c::bdi_get_max_bytes","mm/page-writeback.c::bdi_get_bytes","mm/page-writeback.c::bdi_set_min_bytes","mm/page-writeback.c::bdi_set_max_bytes","mm/page-writeback.c::bdi_check_pages_limit","mm/page-writeback.c::bdi_ratio_from_pages","mm/page-writeback.c::bdi_set_max_ratio","mm/page-writeback.c::__bdi_set_max_ratio","mm/page-writeback.c::bdi_set_max_ratio_no_scale","mm/page-writeback.c::bdi_set_strict_limit","mm/page-writeback.c::bdi_set_min_ratio","mm/page-writeback.c::bdi_set_min_ratio_no_scale","mm/page-writeback.c::__bdi_set_min_ratio","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_put"],"text":"Writeback offers global and cgroup dirty shares, byte and ratio controls validated against dirtyable memory, strict toggles, and parent release on last reference."},{"sids":["mm/backing-dev.c::read_ahead_kb_store","mm/backing-dev.c::BDI_SHOW","mm/backing-dev.c::min_ratio_store","mm/backing-dev.c::min_ratio_fine_store","mm/backing-dev.c::max_ratio_store","mm/backing-dev.c::max_ratio_fine_store","mm/backing-dev.c::min_bytes_store","mm/backing-dev.c::max_bytes_store","mm/backing-dev.c::strict_limit_store","mm/backing-dev.c::min_bytes_show","mm/backing-dev.c::max_bytes_show","mm/backing-dev.c::strict_limit_show","mm/backing-dev.c::stable_pages_required_show","mm/arch_numa.c::debug_cpumask_set_cpu","mm/backing-dev.c::noop_backing_dev_info","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_unknown_name","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_wq"],"text":"Devices expose read-ahead, ratio, byte and strict attributes, per-node CPU debug maps with missing-map diagnostics, defaults, and zero for deprecated stable pages."}],"extracts":["52b8fa3d2d7de102b60185f2ee4dc9a683b1c3704278b29b1c7251d08da271c9","88b4894de213630fe05a3f4b94ba028e365dcbfee61e264e900a02eaa8aac83c","92b1d4c881ba2e9988b6b873e90a323ced32e1f38c05a4837b350857de28866c","a6a2f8f65f767a891389c0d1a6ccdae99811202dea2e8ba9436d8601957325da"],"gpl_spec":"PASS","hazards":[{"sids":["mm/memblock.c::memblock_alloc_range_nid","mm/memblock.c::memblock_search","mm/memblock.c::memblock_search_pfn_nid"],"text":"Late early-allocator calls warn and use slab semantics, zero alignment takes a cache default, and misses return not-found that propagates as unknown node."},{"sids":["mm/percpu.c::pcpu_page_first_chunk","mm/numa_emulation.c::numa_emulation"],"text":"Partial first-chunk pages unwind with error while mapping failure aborts; bad emulation layouts, splits or map repairs abandon cleanly to prior node sets."}],"invariants":[{"sids":["mm/memblock.c::memblock_add_range","mm/memblock.c::memblock_merge_regions","mm/memblock.c::memblock_addrs_overlap","mm/memblock.c::memblock_overlaps_region","mm/memblock.c::memblock_start_of_DRAM","mm/memblock.c::memblock_end_of_DRAM","mm/mm_init.c::__absent_pages_in_range","mm/mm_init.c::absent_pages_in_range","mm/numa_emulation.c::mem_hole_size","mm/mm_init.c::node_map_pfn_alignment"],"text":"Tables stay ordered and disjoint, coalescing only exact matching neighbours; DRAM spans first to last, holes count uncovered pages, and alignment separates nodes."},{"sids":["mm/percpu.c::pcpu_alloc_alloc_info","mm/percpu.c::pcpu_build_alloc_info"],"text":"Per-CPU descriptors store group counts with page-aligned size, preset maps to unassigned, and demand exact unit totals or treat mismatch as fatal."},{"sids":["mm/numa_memblks.c::numa_alloc_distance","mm/numa_memblks.c::numa_set_distance","mm/numa_memblks.c::numa_add_reserved_memblk","mm/numa_memblks.c::numa_reset_distance","mm/numa_memblks.c::numa_clear_kernel_node_hotplug"],"text":"Distances allocate on first use with local/remote prefills and ignore bad writes; overflow diverts to reserved, teardown nulls storage, and kernel nodes shed hotplug marks."},{"sids":["mm/numa_emulation.c::split_nodes_interleave","mm/numa_emulation.c::split_nodes_size_interleave_uniform","mm/numa_emulation.c::split_nodes_size_interleave","mm/numa_emulation.c::find_end_of_node","mm/numa_emulation.c::uniform_size","mm/numa_emulation.c::emu_find_memblk_by_nid","mm/arch_numa.c::numa_emu_dma_end"],"text":"Emulation carves leading prefixes round-robin for count, size and per-node modes, skipping holes and honouring granularity, bounds and remainder rules."},{"sids":["mm/page-writeback.c::global_dirtyable_memory","mm/page-writeback.c::highmem_dirtyable_memory","mm/page-writeback.c::domain_dirty_avail","mm/page-writeback.c::dtc_is_global","mm/page-writeback.c::mdtc_calc_avail","mm/page-writeback.c::__wb_calc_thresh","mm/page-writeback.c::wb_min_max_ratio.alt_1","mm/page-writeback.c::wb_min_max_ratio.alt_2","mm/page-writeback.c::domain_dirty_limits"],"text":"Dirtyable memory nets reserves from free plus cache with highmem fix; member shares avoid double counts and scale by completion with floors, clamps and ordering."},{"sids":["mm/backing-dev.c::wb_update_bandwidth_workfn","mm/page-writeback.c::wb_update_bandwidth","mm/page-writeback.c::__wb_update_bandwidth","mm/page-writeback.c::wb_update_write_bandwidth","mm/page-writeback.c::domain_update_dirty_limit","mm/page-writeback.c::update_dirty_limit","mm/page-writeback.c::dirty_freerun_ceiling","mm/page-writeback.c::hard_dirty_limit","mm/page-writeback.c::wb_update_dirty_ratelimit"],"text":"Bandwidth blends recent with prior over power-of-two windows with flooring and positive floors, limits rise fast but decay slowly, and ratelimits step only when errors agree."}],"locks":[{"sids":["mm/mm_init.c::early_pfn_to_nid","mm/mm_init.c::__early_pfn_to_nid","mm/kmemleak.c::__create_object","mm/kmemleak.c::create_object_phys","mm/kmemleak.c::kmemleak_alloc_phys"],"text":"Node lookup holds an early spinlock across cache and search; leak records allocate unlocked then lock only for linkage, freeing on failure after unlock."},{"sids":["mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_lock","mm/backing-dev.c::collect_wb_stats","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_collect_stats.alt_1","mm/backing-dev.c::cgwb_debug_stats_show"],"text":"A global guard protects ratio shares and strict flags; queue sampling holds list locks for walks with counters outside, and member traversal pairs RCU with references across sleeps."},{"sids":["mm/backing-dev.c::wb_shutdown","mm/backing-dev.c::cgwb_remove_from_bdi_list.alt_1","mm/backing-dev.c::cgwb_remove_from_bdi_list.alt_2","mm/backing-dev.c::cgwb_lock","mm/backing-dev.c::cgwb_release_workfn","mm/backing-dev.c::cgwb_kill","mm/backing-dev.c::wb_exit"],"text":"Per-object locks guard bandwidth, shutdown markers and removals; domain locks pace refresh with rechecked intervals, and cgwb locks guard offline lists with kill requiring held lock."}],"pass":1,"phase_map":[{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p14","crown":"A","phase":"F0"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p04","crown":"A","phase":"F1"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p05","crown":"A","phase":"F3"}],"schema":"lx.dossier.v1","state_machines":[{"sids":["mm/numa_emulation.c::numa_emulation","mm/numa_memblks.c::numa_cleanup_meminfo","mm/arch_numa.c::numa_emu_update_cpu_to_node","mm/numa_emulation.c::setup_emu2phys_nid","mm/numa_memblks.c::numa_set_distance","mm/memblock.c::memblock_alloc_range_nid","mm/percpu.c::pcpu_populate_pte","mm/percpu-vm.c::__pcpu_map_pages"],"text":"Mirrored grants fall back with throttled notice; emulation runs sizing, carving, validation, snapshot, affinity and rebuild with restore on failure; percpu ensures tables and scopes."},{"sids":["mm/backing-dev.c::cgwb_release","mm/backing-dev.c::cgwb_free_rcu","mm/backing-dev.c::cgwb_release_wq","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_put","mm/backing-dev.c::wb_shutdown"],"text":"Teardown queues release work, drops credentials under a mutex, unlinks offline state, drops parent refs and defers frees via RCU, with idempotent shutdown via a marker."},{"sids":["mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_debug_stats_show","mm/backing-dev.c::cgwb_debug_stats_show","mm/backing-dev.c::wb_stats_show","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_collect_stats.alt_1","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_collect_stats.alt_2","mm/backing-dev.c::collect_wb_stats","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_debug_register.alt_1","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_debug_register.alt_2","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_debug_unregister.alt_1","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_debug_unregister.alt_2","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_debug_init.alt_1","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_debug_init.alt_2"],"text":"Stats snapshot limits and aggregate queue counters for device and group views with min-share choice; debug lifecycle builds per-device dirs, stubbed in alternate builds."}],"structs":[{"sids":["mm/numa_memblks.c::numa_remove_memblk_from","mm/numa_memblks.c::numa_add_memblk_to","mm/numa_memblks.c::numa_move_tail_memblk","mm/numa_emulation.c::emu_setup_memblk"],"text":"Memory lists hold counted spans plus nodes with reserved twins; removal shifts tails, emulation consumes prefixes, and bad nodes, overfill or inverted ranges are rejected."},{"sids":["mm/backing-dev.c::wb_stats","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_lock","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_id_cursor","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_tree","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_wq","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_debug_root","mm/page-writeback.c::GDTC_INIT.alt_1","mm/page-writeback.c::GDTC_INIT.alt_2","mm/page-writeback.c::MDTC_INIT.alt_1","mm/page-writeback.c::MDTC_INIT.alt_2","mm/page-writeback.c::mdtc_gdtc.alt_1","mm/page-writeback.c::mdtc_gdtc.alt_2","mm/page-writeback.c::dtc_dom.alt_1","mm/page-writeback.c::dtc_dom.alt_2","mm/backing-dev.c::bdi_dev_attrs","mm/backing-dev.c::INIT_BW","mm/backing-dev.c::wb_init"],"text":"Bookkeeping uses guards, ID trees, workqueues and debug roots with global/member views; tables list controls, per-writeback objects carry lists and stats, and bandwidth seeds to 100MB."}],"stubs":[{"sid":"include/linux/printk.h::pr_info","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D13"},{"sid":"include/linux/printk.h::pr_err","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D13"},{"sid":"include/linux/printk.h::pr_warn","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D13"},{"sid":"include/linux/printk.h::pr_debug.alt_1","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D13"},{"sid":"include/linux/printk.h::pr_warn_once","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D13"},{"sid":"include/linux/debugfs.h::debugfs_create_dir","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D13"},{"sid":"include/linux/debugfs.h::debugfs_create_file.alt_1","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D13"},{"sid":"include/linux/debugfs.h::debugfs_remove_recursive.alt_2","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D13"},{"sid":"include/linux/device.h::dev_get_drvdata","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D13"},{"sid":"include/linux/sysfs.h::sysfs_emit","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D13"},{"sid":"include/linux/minmax.h::min","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D14"},{"sid":"include/linux/minmax.h::max","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D14"},{"sid":"include/linux/minmax.h::clamp","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D14"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bitops/builtin-__ffs.h::__ffs","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D14"},{"sid":"include/linux/math.h::roundup","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D14"},{"sid":"include/linux/math64.h::div64_ul.alt_1","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D14"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bitops/instrumented-atomic.h::test_and_clear_bit","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D14"},{"sid":"include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_read","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D14"},{"sid":"include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_set","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D14"},{"sid":"include/linux/fortify-string.h::memset","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/linux/fortify-string.h::memmove","state":"stub","target_dossier